.TH MCP 7 "July 2025" "VeilOS 0.6" "VeilOS Miscellaneous Information"
.SH NAME
mcp \- The VeilOS Model Context Protocol
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Model Context Protocol (MCP) is a simple, read-only HTTP interface that allows VeilOS to serve its live internal state to other AI models or external applications. This protocol is the key to enabling VeilOS to act as a "conductor" for a swarm of other specialized AI agents.
.P
By exposing its World State Model (WSM) as a JSON object, VeilOS can provide rich, real-time context to other models, allowing them to perform tasks with a greater understanding of the user's goals and the system's current state.
.SH USAGE
The MCP server is started automatically on boot and runs on a predefined local port.
.TP
.B Endpoint
.BR /context
.TP
.B Method
.BR GET
.TP
.B Response
A JSON object representing the complete, live World State Model.
.SH EXAMPLE
An external script or AI agent can make an HTTP GET request to \fBhttp://localhost:8686/context\fP to retrieve the current state of VeilOS.
.P
.I curl http://localhost:8686/context
.SH SECURITY
The MCP server is bound to localhost by default and is read-only, providing a secure way to share state without exposing control of the OS.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR veil (1),
.BR wsm (7)
